{"author": "pgaudet", "body": "Dear all, \n\nThe proposal has been made to obsolete \n- 'pyruvate dehydrogenase activity (GO:0004738)' - unnecessary grouping term (7 direct EXP annotations to check/move)\n- 'pyruvate dehydrogenase [NAD(P)+] activity (GO:0034603)' - unnecessary grouping term (no direct annotations to worry about)\n- 'pyruvate dehydrogenase (NAD+) activity (GO:0034604)' - combination of 3 reactions in the PDH complex; already represented by the BP term GO:0006086 pyruvate decarboxylation to acetyl-CoA\n- GO:1904182 regulation of pyruvate dehydrogenase activity - policy is to obsolete \"regulation of activity\" in the BP branch\n\n\nsee https://github.com/geneontology/go-ontology/issues/24350\n\nAnnotations are here: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Wp5h-khwOtI0SlXPbUBQ2DqaNgmbZ_9glEfxJbxE_WI/edit?gid=0#gid=0\n\nGroup | Number of annotations | Status\n-- | -- | --\nEcoliWiki | 2 | \nMGI | 14  | \nPomBase | 1  | \nSGD | 1  |  DONE\nUniProt | 2  |  DONE\nZFIN | 2  | \n\n\n\n\nThanks.\n", "created_at": "2025-04-02T11:30:50Z", "key": "issue", "labels": ["annotation review", "direct_ann_to_list_of_terms"], "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "title": "Review annotations to pyruvate dehydrogenase activity GO:0004738 & children", "type": "issue", "updated_at": "2025-04-15T15:42:55Z"}
